From eccceb6e8cb1cad876509f88a80a0deb548ac44f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:08:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Verify source signatures with openpgpverify

Replace the direct GnuPG verification with %openpgpverify, which
uses Sequoia sqv, as part of the Fedora 45 Change
https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Changes/Sequoia_openpgpverify

Refresh keyring.gpg from keyservers/WKD: same certificate(s), with self-
signatures our copy was missing; the commands are in the spec comment.
The GnuPG keybox becomes a plain OpenPGP keyring, which sqv can read.
Release bumped with a changelog entry.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 keyring.gpg   | Bin 4556 -> 8104 bytes
 pyparted.spec |  12 ++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

